WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:06.300
Good radio habits make you sound like a professional, and more important, they make you understood.

2
00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:09.675
Use the phonetic alphabet to spell things out.

3
00:00:09.925 --> 00:00:12.500
Alfa, Bravo, Charlie, Delta.

4
00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:16.850
On a crackling radio, B and D and E all sound alike.

5
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.475
Say over when you want a reply.

6
00:00:19.725 --> 00:00:22.500
Say out when the conversation is finished.

7
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.850
And over and out together?

8
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.650
It makes no sense.

9
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.700
It means, reply to me, I’m finished.

10
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:36.100
Radio checks go on a working channel, or an automated radio-check service.

11
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:38.350
Never on sixteen.

12
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:43.725
Make your first call on sixteen or nine, then move to a working channel to talk.

13
00:00:43.975 --> 00:00:48.875
Sixteen is for calling and for distress, not for chatting about the bite.

14
00:00:49.125 --> 00:00:51.675
And never make a false distress call.

15
00:00:51.925 --> 00:00:57.150
It’s a federal crime, and it can cost you fines, prison, and the bill for the search.
